  "reason": "KB-005 quick check: confirm departed employee account status (read-only)"
}

{
  "user_id": 10,
  "reason": "KB-005 quick check: review sign-in attempts on disabled former-employee account for security review"
}

{
  "summary": "P1 security. Reported by Priya Nair (IT Manager, priya.nair@brightline.example): she's getting failed-login alerts on former employee Ryan Brooks' account (user_id 10, ryan.brooks@brightline.example, Sales AE, left in spring). Checks so far (read-only): account status = disabled, password last set 2026-03-23. BUT sign_in_blocked = false and vpn_access = TRUE, so offboarding looks incomplete. Sign-in logs: 2 failed_password VPN attempts on 2026-10-09 at 07:05 and 07:07 UTC (03:05/03:07 ET, outside his usual hours) from IP 192.0.2.140, a hosting network in Amsterdam, NL. No MFA was involved and nothing succeeded. This looks like someone trying stolen or old credentials against VPN. Tier 1 has not reset, unlocked, or blocked anything: per KB-005, Tier 1 doesn't act on another user's or a disabled account. Still needed: security review; confirm VPN really rejects a disabled account and revoke vpn_access / set sign-in block; block IP 192.0.2.140; check for other attempts from this IP on other accounts; finish offboarding for this account (sessions, tokens, device BL-LT-0110).",
  "reason": "KB-005 says always escalate; ticket is P1; hosting-network attempts on a disabled account that still has VPN access"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Priya, thanks for flagging this. I checked Ryan Brooks' account. It's disabled, but VPN access is still turned on for it. Early this morning (around 3:05 and 3:07 AM Eastern) someone made two VPN sign-in attempts from a hosting provider in Amsterdam. Both failed because of a wrong password, and neither got in. I haven't changed anything on Ryan's account myself. I've sent this to Tier 2 and security as a high-priority issue so they can turn off the leftover VPN access, block the source address, and finish closing down the account. They'll follow up with you directly.",
  "internal_note": "Sender: Priya Nair, IT Manager (user_id 3). Target: Ryan Brooks (user_id 10), former Sales AE. Read-only checks only. Status is disabled, but sign_in_blocked=false and vpn_access=true, so offboarding looks incomplete. Sign-in logs: 2 failed_password VPN attempts on 2026-10-09 at 07:05 and 07:07 UTC (03:05 ET, outside his usual hours) from 192.0.2.140, a hosting network in Amsterdam, NL. No MFA involved, nothing succeeded. Following KB-005, I did not reset, unlock, or block anything because this isn't the sender's account. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation id 1) as P1, recommending: revoke VPN access and set a sign-in block, block the IP, check other accounts for attempts from this IP, and finish offboarding (sessions, tokens, device BL-LT-0110).",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-005"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
